    <DataNode elementId="AT5G17050-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G17050-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LFJ8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1050" centerY="595" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The At5g17050 gene has been found to encode a flavonoid 3-O-glucosyltransferase in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; introducing a glucose group to the 3-position of the flavonoid C-ring. The gene was induced in response to plants overexpressing the PAP1 gene encoding an MYB transcription factor. Homozygote mutants bearing T-DNA insertions of the gene did not produce the protein and were found to contain significantly less anthocyanins than the wild type. The molecular function was confirmed by expressing recombinant proteins in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The enzyme accepted both anthocyanidins (cyanidin, pelargonidin and delphinidin) and flavonols (kaempferol, quercetin and myricetin) and converted them to the corresponding 3-O-glucosides. The enzyme also accepted flavonoids which have not been found in Arabidopsis (delphinidin, myricetin) |CITS: [15807784]|. The molecular function of At5g17050 as flavonoid/anthocyanin 3-O-glucosyltransferase was confirmed using the anthocyaninless1 (anl1) mutant of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; which showed a dramatic loss of glucosylated anthocyanin. The gene At5g17050 was expressed in all tissues investigated such as rosette leaves, stems, flower buds and roots |CITS:[17277900]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G17050-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G17050.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9LFJ8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAL61932.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9LFJ8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR002213" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00201" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11926" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Cazy" value="GT1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9LFJ8" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS00375" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-24807, RXN-12567, RXN-82, RXN-12672, RXN-12671" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="5" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G17050.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G17050" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15807784" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17277900" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT4G34135-MONOMER" textLabel="flavonol 3-O-glucosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G34135.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="675" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding a flavonol 3-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-glucosyltransferase (AtGT-1) was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. Its molecular function of attaching glucose to the 3-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-position of the C-ring was confirmed as recombinant protein expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. However, although the enzyme preferred to glucosylate the 3-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-position of flavonols such as kaempferol, quercetin and isorhamnetin, flavonoids missing the 3-hydroxyl group such as the flavanones eriodictyol and naringenin or the flavones luteolin and apigenin were glucosylated with high efficiency at the 7-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-position of the A-ring |CITS: [KIM06]|. In contrary to the reported substrate specificity of this enzyme another author reported the characterization of an enzyme encoded by the same locus (At4g34135) that has been specific for the 7-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-position (A-ring) of flavonols, flavanones and flavones but also had a lower affinity to glucosylate the 3-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-position (C-ring) of kaempferol and quercetin, eventually also forming the flavonol 3,5-diglucosides |CITS: [14697269]|. The reversed position preference of the two reported enzymes originating from the same locus remains to be validated but may reflect the low substrate specificity of that glucosyltransferase (UGT73B2). Additional information: The Arabidopsis locus At4g34135 consists of two splice variants (At4g34135.1 and At4g34135.2)</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G34135-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G34135.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAR01231" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33443, RXN-15418, RXN-15426, RXN-15440, RXN-15446, RXN-15432, RXN-13130, RXN-13131, RXN-13132, RXN-13127, RXN-13128, RXN-13129" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="12" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G34135.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G34135" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_KIM06" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_14697269" />
    </DataNode>
